From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 15 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.283
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.283 V19.0.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  MCPTT-ID (4500): UTF8String, clause 7.3.2
  Data-Identification (4501): Grouped, 2 members, clause 7.3.3
  Data-Identification-Prefix (4502): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.11
  Data-Identification-Flags (4503): Unsigned64, clause 7.3.12
  DPR-Flags (4504): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.13
  DPA-Flags (4505): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.14
  DUR-Flags (4506): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.15
  DUA-Flags (4507): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.16
  NDR-Flags (4508): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.17
  NDA-Flags (4509): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.18
  User-Data-Id (4510): Unsigned32, clause 7.3.19
  MC-Service-User-Profile-Data (4511): Grouped, 3 members, clause 7.3.20
  Data (4513): Grouped, 1 member, clause 7.3.22
  MCVideo-ID (4514): UTF8String, clause 7.3.24
  MCData-ID (4515): UTF8String, clause 7.3.25

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Not added here: Sequence-Number, code 4512, named like the dictionary's
code 716 of vendor 10415. Wireshark names each display filter field
after its AVP, so two entries named alike need one renamed, as
Cx-User-Data and Sh-User-Data are.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..5bed091 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -7971,6 +7971,60 @@
 				<gavp name="Type-Of-External-Identifier"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="MCPTT-ID" code="4500" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="Data-Identification" code="4501" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="Data-Identification-Prefix"/>
+				<gavp name="Data-Identification-Flags"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="Data-Identification-Prefix" code="4502" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="Data-Identification-Flags" code="4503" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned64"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="DPR-Flags" code="4504" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="DPA-Flags" code="4505" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="DUR-Flags" code="4506" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="DUA-Flags" code="4507" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="NDR-Flags" code="4508" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="NDA-Flags" code="4509" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="User-Data-Id" code="4510" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="MC-Service-User-Profile-Data" code="4511" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="Sh-User-Data"/>
